  "description" : "[h1]Quick Select[/h1]\nAdds a hotkey to pick the block you're looking at from your own inventory similarly to an eyedropper/pipette. Doesn't move or create new items in your inventory, it just instantly selects what's under your cursor. Makes building SO much easier and without cheats.\n\n[h2]Hotkey[/h2]\n- Smart mode: Default is [b]\"V\"[/b]\n- Classic mode: Unassigned\n- Can be changed from the \"Mod Binds\" menu in \"Options\".\n\n[h2]Compatibility[/h2]\n[b][u]This mod requires [url=https://github.com/OpenStarbound/OpenStarbound]OpenStarbound[/url] in order to function.[/u][/b]\n\nMay not be compatible with mods that modify the inventory system (not just its appearance) nothing should [b]break[/b] though. But... I made out-of-the-box patches for the following mods:\n\n- [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=882900100]bk3k's Inventory[/url], any version.\n- [url=http://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=853665529]Bigger Action Bar[/url], any version.\n- [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=729480149]Frackin' Universe[/url] and most mods that just add content.\n- Any mod that adds custom bags.\n- If it doesn't work with some mod you really like, I can try to fix it.\n\n[h2]Planned[/h2]\n- Liquids are [i]currently[/i] not supported.\n- Alt-hand support. If you have one-handed torches, they currently go into a new slot even if the secondary hand is available.\n- Search in multiple hotbars at once (the ones you cycle with \"X\")\n\nWill implement these soon. Probably...\n\n[h2]Uninstall!!!??[/h2]\n- Unsubscribe, done. \n- No lingering garbage.\n\n[b]What's the difference between smart and classic mode? [/b]\n- Smart mode tries not to replace your tools and other useful items in your hotbar. \nPicking blocks will search for other blocks in your hotbar first, picking decorations/crafting stations will look for similar items, etc. \n- Classic mode just replaces what you're currently holding if there are not empty slots.\n\nHere's the [url=https://github.com/notSagyo/quick-select]GitHub repo[/url]. It's under MIT license, so do whatever you want with it.",
